From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gerson Fernando Budke <gerson.budke@ossystems.com.br>
Subject: [PATCH] STM32_ADC_Common: Fix watchdog 2/3 bits

The watchdog 2 and 3 can selected by the channel bit. This reserves the
bits to match with the number of channels.

Signed-off-by: Gerson Fernando Budke <gerson.budke@ossystems.com.br>

Ported to Renode v1.17.0 STM32_ADC_Common API.
Upstream already sizes AWDxCH by the channel count; only the reserved
bits width is fixed so that bit 31 is covered as well.

diff --git a/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/Analog/STM32_ADC_Common.cs b/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/Analog/STM32_ADC_Common.cs
--- a/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/Analog/STM32_ADC_Common.cs
+++ b/src/Emulator/Peripherals/Peripherals/Analog/STM32_ADC_Common.cs
@@ @@ private void BuildWatchdogRegisters(Dictionary<long, DoubleWordRegister> registe
                 {
                     registers.Add((long)GetConfigurationRegister(i), new DoubleWordRegister(this)
                         .WithFlags(0, ADCChannelCount, out var selectedChannels, name: $"AWD{i + 1}CH")
-                        .WithReservedBits(ADCChannelCount, 31 - ADCChannelCount));
+                        .WithReservedBits(ADCChannelCount, 32 - ADCChannelCount));
                     analogWatchdogSelectedChannels.Add(i, selectedChannels);
                 }
             }
